n": 30, "color": "W", "move": "H2", "lead_before": -17.48, "lead_after": -13.75, "points_lost": 3.73, "best": "D2"}, {"turn": 31, "color": "B", "move": "H5", "lead_before": -13.75, "lead_after": -20.39, "points_lost": 6.64, "best": "D2"}, {"turn": 32, "color": "W", "move": "J3", "lead_before": -20.39, "lead_after": -13.88, "points_lost": 6.5, "best": "D1"}, {"turn": 33, "color": "B", "move": "J4", "lead_before": -13.88, "lead_after": -18.11, "points_lost": 4.23, "best": "D2"}, {"turn": 34, "color": "W", "move": "J2", "lead_before": -18.11, "lead_after": -13.85, "points_lost": 4.26, "best": "D2"}, {"turn": 35, "color": "B", "move": "J6", "lead_before": -13.85, "lead_after": -17.5, "points_lost": 3.65, "best": "D2"}, {"turn": 36, "color": "W", "move": "J7", "lead_before": -17.5, "lead_after": -14.2, "points_lost": 3.31, "best": "D2"}, {"turn": 37, "color": "B", "move": "H7", "lead_before": -14.2, "lead_after": -13.85, "points_lost": -0.35, "best": "H7"}, {"turn": 38, "color": "W", "move": "J5", "lead_before": -13.85, "lead_after": -13.95, "points_lost": -0.1, "best": "J5"}, {"turn": 39, "color": "B", "move": "J8", "lead_before": -13.95, "lead_after": -17.85, "points_lost": 3.9, "best": "D2"}, {"turn": 40, "color": "W", "move": "J6", "lead_before": -17.85, "lead_after": -17.87, "points_lost": -0.02, "best": "H4"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "A Gap Filled, a Lead Never Found", "summary": "The 16k won when Opus 5.5 resigned at move 41, trailing by 17.9 points. Opus 5.5 was already behind by 6.2 after move 7, and D7 at move 13 cost 6.1 more. Later both sides kept giving points back, but the 16k's mean loss was lower (1.4 against 2.3 per move) and the lead never came back within reach.", "moments": [{"turn": 7, "text": "E7 lost 2.5 points and dropped Black's lead from -3.6 to -6.2. The engine wanted D4 here, and it kept preferring D4 on moves 8 and 9 too. Black's stones were climbing the sixth and seventh lines while White took the middle."}, {"turn": 11, "text": "D4 was the engine's own first choice, and it gained 0.6 points (-6.3 to -5.8). It was the point the engine had been asking for since move 7, and it made a solid pair with D5. It was too late to close the gap, but it was the best-looking move of the middle game."}, {"turn": 13, "text": "D7 lost 6.1 points, the biggest swing of the early game, taking the lead from -6.2 to -12.3. It filled in between C7 and E7 while White's stones on E8, F7 and F6 stood close by. The engine preferred G5. White's D8 reply lost 2.1 but left Black still far behind."}, {"turn": 31, "text": "H5 extended Black's wall along row 5 and lost 6.6 points, Opus 5.5's worst move, sending the lead from -13.8 to -20.4. White's stones on E2 through H2 stood below it, and the engine's pick was D2."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "J3 was the 16k's worst move, losing 6.5 points, and it handed back almost everything H5 had cost: the lead went from -20.4 to -13.9. Even so, Black was still more than thirteen points behind with the board nearly full."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and uses flood fill to print each group's stones, liberty count and a danger flag for groups with two or fewer liberties. It describes the current position, does not choose or rank moves, and does not look ahead.", "stop": false}}